          "kind": "points",
          "url": "tarn-taran/fires.geojson",
          "description": "Each dot is one VIIRS fire detection: a 375 m pixel that a satellite flagged as holding at least one fire at the time of its pass, drawn at the pixel's centre. It is not a fire's exact place, its size or a count of burning fields, and fires that burn between passes or under thick smoke or cloud can be missed.",
          "method": "VIIRS 375 m active fire detections from NASA FIRMS (area API; sources VIIRS_NOAA20_NRT, VIIRS_NOAA21_NRT, VIIRS_SNPP_NRT) with UTC dates from 2026-09-15 to 2026-11-14, inside the site box. A detection found in two sources (same satellite, UTC date and time, latitude and longitude) is kept once, from the source listed first (0 dropped). Coordinates rounded to 5 decimals. Details: docs/METHODS.md, section 6.",
